      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be really cool idea for example, having a portal in one world change the spawn location in another (so everyone coming from one world would appear in a different place than those entering from the worlds menu). Would allow for a sort of game spectation, and a lot of other cool ideas that aren't covered by the persistence system.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-12-29T11:09:40.129Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I wish vrchat had the ability to pass variables much like HTTP parameters in portals, so that when users are playing a game and the game wants to pass data from one world instance to another it can. Ideally this would be implemented so that it can be controlled by the SDK but also so that it works as regular HTTP parameters that could be passed into the world so when the world HTTP link is sent to somebody it can carry some data with it.\nSo for example imagine you wanted to pass state about the users health or potentially items they're carrying or whatever.\nMy specific use case is I'd like to be able to have the user go through a portal and transfer data about what the user is carrying from one world to another.\nThe other component of this which is captured in other feature requests already mentioned is the ability to specify the instance ID and then the ability to retrieve the instance ID from the SDK so that users can be directed to and return to worlds they were previously in.",
